Give every Git worktree a durable identity, an isolated home, and a routed URL.

Usage:
  treerig [flags]
  treerig [command]

Start here
  init        write a starter treerig.toml at the repository root
  up          register this worktree, start its services, and run its hooks

Day to day
  dev         start this worktree's services, then follow their logs until
              Ctrl-C
  down        stop this worktree's services; data is kept
  status      show service status for this worktree
  urls        print this worktree's routed URLs
  worktree    manage registered worktrees

Project tasks
  run         run one of the project's named commands from treerig.toml
              [commands]
  backup      run the backup hook, writing a bundle into a directory
  restore     run the restore hook on a bundle directory
  route       route processes running on the host through this worktree's
              hostname

Problems
  doctor      check prerequisites, the registry, the router, and this checkout's
              verify hook

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for treerig
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
  -V, --version         output the version number

Use "treerig [command] --help" for more information about a command.
Use "treerig help --all" for shared services, the router, configuration, the
teardown pin and completion.
